 "url": "issues/daily/2026/11/2026-11-21.html",
 "subject": "Claude can now work in the apps on your work computer",
 "preview": "Also: a coding agent's leaked key exposed customer prompts, Lean's community certifies the Claude-assisted Riemann proof, Teams agents face a deadline on file access, and Signal shuts out phone agents.",
 "body": "<!-- buttondown-editor-mode: fancy -->\n<div style=\"display:none;max-height:0;overflow:hidden;mso-hide:all\">Also: a coding agent&#x27;s leaked key exposed customer prompts, Lean&#x27;s community certifies the Claude-assisted Riemann proof, Teams agents face a deadline on file access, and Signal shuts out phone agents.&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;</div>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">News from Saturday, November 21, 2026 · <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/issues/daily/2026/11/2026-11-21.html\">Read on the web</a></p>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">What matters today</h2>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/covers/2026-11-21-0.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"Claude Desktop asking to turn on computer use, listing the apps Claude wants to use and the access each gets\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><p style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">Image: <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://claude.com/blog/dispatch-and-computer-use\">Anthropic</a></p><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">Claude uses work computers</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12138966-release-notes\">Anthropic opens Claude computer use to Team and Enterprise plans</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>In beta since November 20:</strong> Claude sees the screen and clicks and types in the desktop apps a user allows. It is <strong>off by default</strong> and reaches companies gradually.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Admin controls:</strong> owners turn it on and can limit it to roles and to chosen apps. Anthropic warns there is <strong>no sandbox</strong>: a web page or email on screen could steer Claude.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>An admin switch now decides which apps an agent may touch, the way IT approves software. Apps without a connector still get used by agents, so their screens join what a company signs off on.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/art/2026-11-21-1.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">Teams tightens agents' file access</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoftteams/platform/bots/how-to/bots-filesv4#update-an-existing-bot-to-authenticate-file-requests\">Microsoft changes how Teams agents get to files</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Action required:</strong> agents that send or receive files in Teams must update by <strong>March 1, 2027</strong>; after that, a token from a client secret gets refused. Announced November 20.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Permissions:</strong> from January 15, 2027, agents also declare file permissions in their app manifest, in line with OneDrive and SharePoint sign-in rules.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Microsoft now treats an agent's file access like an app's: declared up front and approved. Agents in Teams get a deadline, and admins get a clearer view of which files each agent can touch.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/covers/2026-11-21-2.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"Together AI&#x27;s logo on its Security event title art\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><p style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">Image: <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://www.together.ai/blog/security-event-prompt-leakage-for-requests-in-june-and-july-of-2026\">Together AI</a></p><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">A coding agent leaks a key</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.together.ai/blog/security-event-prompt-leakage-for-requests-in-june-and-july-of-2026\">Together AI says stored customer prompts were stolen</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>How:</strong> an AI coding agent put a credential in a public GitHub repository. Someone used it to download <strong>prompt samples from June and July</strong> and search them for passwords.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Fixes:</strong> no data retention by default for new accounts, short-lived credentials, secret checks on every pull request, new rules for coding agents.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Wider:</strong> on November 22, <a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://openrouter.ai/blog/announcements/data-processing-incidents-on-inference-providers/\">OpenRouter</a> dropped three providers after researchers' leak tests.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>The leak came from a coding agent holding secrets, not from the model. Prompts are customer data, so keeping none becomes the default buyers expect, not a premium promise.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/art/2026-11-21-3.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">Claude and the Riemann proof</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://alpo.ge/remark.pdf\">An Anthropic mathematician posts a Riemann proof made with Claude</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>November 20:</strong> Levent Alpöge says it covers the <strong>Generalized</strong> Riemann Hypothesis, and that he and Claude wrote it out in the Lean proof checker.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>November 21:</strong> <a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/blog/posts/riemann-hypothesis/\">Lean's community certifies</a> the 17 million-line proof; checkers that <strong>cannot accept a false proof</strong> passed it.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>The proof was trusted within a day because a machine could check it, not because anyone trusted the AI behind it. AI work that carries checkable evidence wins trust faster.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/covers/2026-11-21-4.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"Signal&#x27;s iOS settings with a Block Siri AI switch turned on under App Security\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><p style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">Image: <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://signal.org/blog/protecting-your-privacy/\">Signal</a></p><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">Signal blocks phone agents</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://signal.org/blog/protecting-your-privacy/\">Signal stops AI assistants built into phones from reading its screen</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Since November 20:</strong> screenshots are blocked in the app on iOS 27, and on Android when an AI assistant tries to capture the screen. Users can turn the protection off in settings.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Why:</strong> Signal says Apple, Google and Microsoft give apps <strong>no easy way to keep these agents out</strong>, which is also why it cannot do the same on macOS yet.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Agents that work by reading the screen now meet apps that refuse them. If more apps follow, agent builders will need a permitted way into each app instead of screenshots.</p></div>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Research worth watching</h2>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 18px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://metr.org/blog/2026-11-20-q4-2026-capability-update/\">AI matches skilled engineers, not their judgment</a></p><p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\">METR finds models usually match or beat skilled humans on its coding tasks, with time horizons <strong>doubling about every 3.6 months</strong>, but judge worse than experts when feedback is unclear.</p><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Let agents run work that has clear tests; keep people on calls that tests cannot check.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 18px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://frontier.replit.com/throwing-headcount-at-the-problem/\">When 32 agents beat one</a></p><p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\">On NumPy, a swarm of <strong>32 Claude Opus 5.5 agents</strong> made the code 18.9x faster in two hours, against 3.7x for one. The best swarms shared a common board instead of routing through a coordinator.</p><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>More agents pay off only when the work splits cleanly and they share what they learn.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 18px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2611.25200\">Simulated shoppers call A/B test winners</a></p><p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\">A model trained on real browsing simulated 1,000 shoppers per version and called <strong>267 of 318</strong> past website tests right (84%), against 61.6% for the best general model.</p><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Teams could screen ideas first and spend live traffic only on likely winners.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 18px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://www.minimax.io/blog/practical-cryptanalysis-with-minimaxs-latest-internal-model\">An AI finds working attacks on encryption</a></p><p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\">MiniMax's unreleased model built practical breaks of past NIST candidates and recovered keys for <strong>55 previously unsolved</strong> McEliece challenges; MiniMax says deployed standards are unaffected.</p><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>When a model's attack either works or fails, its research claims can be checked, not just trusted.</p></div>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">What developers are debating</h2>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 12px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://architectlabs.com/blog/frostbite\">Frostbite, a CPU designed by AI</a>: developers argued over a chip whose makers say AI designed and verified it end to end, with 645 points and 333 comments.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 12px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://github.com/ShinMegamiBoson/lookatmyquant\">Inkling 2 Mini in 5.4 GB</a>: a shrunken build of Thinking Machines' small coding model that fits in 5.4 GB of memory drew 458 points and 114 comments.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 12px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://manidoraisamy.com/developer-to-architect.html\">Developers became architects</a>: an essay on code written by AI that works but makes needless calls, and who now has to catch it, drew 425 points and 235 comments.</p>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Top launches yesterday</h2>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/046485e6-d8fe-4168-8047-978bd2b33c83.png?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://altercontacts.ai/\">AlterContacts</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">An assistant for client-facing advisors that files what you say after a meeting under the right client, tracks promises and drafts follow-ups for you to approve.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/4a36951e-d17a-4da4-9569-c87e9b3c7c8f.png?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://plurality.network/ai-context-flow\">AI Context Flow MCP</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">One shared memory that ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini and other MCP tools can all read, with access control and version history.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/3e50a01b-e3db-4b0b-a49f-703cc6f0790a.png?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://codemany.com/\">Codemany</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">Runs GitHub Actions jobs on your own Mac or Linux machines, a fresh virtual machine per job, with no per-minute billing.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/launch-image-uploads/165a790f-cb14-4ecf-8188-0976f892913c/df3ba31e637be461c170f2c658214b3f622c5aba15dfb796f7ed5cf31b5a8aaf.png?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://glassmail.app/\">Glassmail</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">A native Mac email app for Gmail, iCloud and Outlook whose AI runs on the device, sold for a one-time price.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/73cc34e6-a8d6-4b26-8cad-4abcb07f3a28.jpeg?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://exa.ai/blog/websets-v2\">Exa Websets V2</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">Builds a dataset from the live web out of a plain-language description, with the source and reasoning for each row.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/21766723-2ed5-428e-8814-137a48095fb9.svg?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://openvorld.com/\">OpenVorld</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">An open-source harness that shows coding agents such as Claude Code or Codex as a village, each asking before it uses a folder, command or website.</div></td></tr></table>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Also in the news</h2>\n<ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/6825453-chatgpt-release-notes\"><strong>ChatGPT Space</strong></a>: since November 20, rolling out to Plus users 18 and older on web, desktop, iOS and Android; it replaces Library with pages and decks that can update from connected apps.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/news/ipo-close\"><strong>Anthropic IPO closes</strong></a>: November 20; about $93.5 billion raised at $83 a share, plus a $26.0 billion private sale to AMD, Broadcom, Google, Micron, Microsoft, Nvidia and TSMC.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://openai.com/index/combatting-adversarial-distillation\"><strong>OpenAI on copying</strong></a>: November 20; attacks that recover a model's hidden reasoning succeeded 0.2% of the time against GPT-6.2 Astra, down from 54.0% against GPT-6 Astra.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://developers.googleblog.com/check-what-your-ai-agents-do-before-they-do-it-with-semantic-governance-policies/\"><strong>Google agent rules</strong></a>: November 20; in preview, each tool call an agent proposes is checked against the user's request and rules written in plain language.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/11/agent-registry-naming-public-discovery/\"><strong>AWS Agent Registry</strong></a>: November 20; agents can carry a verified domain name and be found by any AWS user, so others can confirm who runs an agent before connecting.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/11/aws-quick-enterprise-guardrails-preview/\"><strong>AWS Quick guardrails</strong></a>: November 20; in preview, admins block prompts by topic, word or personal data, per user or group, with a test mode that only logs matches.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://kiro.dev/blog/kiro-for-vs-code\"><strong>Kiro for VS Code</strong></a>: November 20; Amazon's coding agent is generally available as a VS Code extension and reads the same project setup as the Kiro IDE.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/foundry/managed-compute-ga/\"><strong>Foundry Managed Compute</strong></a>: November 20; generally available; Microsoft runs 150+ open models on dedicated GPUs.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.theverge.com/policy/1038892/trump-foreign-data-centers-tax\"><strong>Data center tax</strong></a>: November 20; Trump threatened a \"tremendous tax\" on US companies that build data centers abroad, without details.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://technode.com/2026/11/20/tencent-releases-hy4-model-weights-with-million-token-context/\"><strong>Tencent Hy4</strong></a>: November 20; flagship weights under Apache 2.0, 770 billion parameters. The team <a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://pandaily.com/tencent-hy-ama-larger-models-flash-lite-24gb-roadmap\">says</a> its next model will be substantially larger.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://thinkingmachines.ai/news/inkling-2-mini/\"><strong>Inkling 2 Mini</strong></a>: November 20; Thinking Machines releases open weights of a coding model that needs about 20GB of memory, enough for a laptop.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://pandaily.com/tencent-workbuddy-computer-use-public-beta-desktop-apps\"><strong>WorkBuddy</strong></a>: Tencent's office agent can click and type in Windows and Mac apps with no API, in public beta since November 20.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/meta-ads-is-now-available-in-aws-quick/\"><strong>Meta ads in AWS Quick</strong></a>: through Meta's ads MCP server, Quick can analyze, create and edit campaigns and budgets in plain language; available now.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://cryptobriefing.com/amazon-nears-deal-ai-startup-decart/\"><strong>Amazon and Decart</strong></a>: Amazon is reportedly near a $7.5 billion deal for the Israeli world-model startup, whose tools help models train on Amazon's own chips; it could close early next week.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.theverge.com/tech/1039554/un-regulations-killer-robots\"><strong>Autonomous weapons</strong></a>: UN talks in Geneva ended with countries agreeing to \"start discussing options\" and two years to propose rules, some of which may stay optional.</li></ul>\n<hr style=\"border:0;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;margin:32px 0 16px\">\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">You get the AI Brief because you subscribed at <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/\">ai.mediancanadian.ca</a>. <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"{{ unsubscribe_url }}\">Unsubscribe</a> at any time; it takes effect at once.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">The AI Brief is from The Median Canadian. Contact: <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"mailto:info@mediancanadian.ca\">info@mediancanadian.ca</a>. <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/privacy.html\">Privacy</a>.</p>\n",
